{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["He said <b>and YHWH spoke.</b> [This introduces] the law of the one being purified. Rabbi Jonah the Spaniard, the grammarian, said that 'when the plague of tzara'at is healed from the metzora' is inverted, and it ought to be 'when the metzora is healed from the plague of tzara'at.' But why should we invert the words of the living Elohim on account of our lack of understanding? Is it not written there, 'when the netek is healed, it is pure,' and furthermore, 'when the plague is healed'?"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:59.292506950Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}